# Build a Loremaster, hand him tomes, and read what they give him. That is
# bd inc-tek.8.3 finding PA-03-F10: "Bibliographic Insight", the class's
# 5th-level ability, had no implementation of any kind.
#
# The prose promises "an extra +1d2 attribute points from any tome they read"
# (lib/prestige.irh:2052-2053) and the level table lists the ability at 5th.
# The Grants block jumped from 3rd level to 6th, the class's EV_ADVANCE
# handler branched only on levels 2, 4 and 8, and a search for
# "Bibliographic" across lib/ found nothing but the table row.
#
# THE FIX is not in the class, because it cannot be: the attribute gain
# happens inside each tome's own EV_MAGIC_HIT handler, which calls
# GainInherentBonus with e.vDmg. A grant on the class cannot reach into that
# roll, so the bonus is added where the roll is consumed -- in all seven
# tomes, one per attribute (lib/m_items.irh).
#
# THE ORACLE is the character sheet's attribute line, which itemises where
# each point came from: "STR: 16/00 [+3/+2] (base 13, +3 inherent)".
# GainInherentBonus is what writes that "+N inherent" term.
#
# THE BUILD. The gate (lib/prestige.irh:1972-2010) wants four Knowledge
# skills at 10, ten levels of known Divination spells, the Scribe Scroll feat
# and a neutral component in the alignment. A mage carries every Knowledge
# skill, and wizard mode's Learn Any Spell supplies the four Divination
# spells by name so that nothing depends on which spells a seed offers.
# Mage 5 plus Loremaster 5 is 10 levels, inside the cap of 11.

a       # Initial Choices: [a] Create a New Character
n       # Alter the character generation options? -- no
y       # Your options will place the game in Explore Mode. Continue? -- yes

@choose "Human"
@choose "Knowledge (Planes)"    # humans choose two bonus skills
@while "Choose a skill:" a
@choose "Mage"

# Point buy, 75 points, spent to the last one.
p
RIGHT*5         # STR 13
DOWN
RIGHT*8         # DEX 16
DOWN
RIGHT*8         # CON 16
DOWN
RIGHT*10        # INT 18
DOWN
RIGHT*8         # WIS 16
DOWN
RIGHT*7         # CHA 15
DOWN
RIGHT*10        # LUC 18
ENTER y         # "Are these your final stats?"

@choose "Neutral"               # the gate wants a neutral component
@choose "Divination"            # the wizard specialty
# Scribe Scroll is not chosen here, and must not be: a mage is given it at
# 1st level already (lib/classes.irh:870), so it never appears on the feat
# list at all.
@while "Choose a feat" a

@expect "Unspent Skill Ranks"
@cursorto:mark "Knowledge (Planes" DOWN
RIGHT*3
@cursorto:mark "Knowledge (Magic" UP
RIGHT*3
@cursorto:mark "Knowledge (Mytho" DOWN
RIGHT*3
@cursorto:mark "Knowledge (Nature" DOWN
RIGHT*3
@cursorto:mark "Alchemy" UP
RIGHT*3
@cursorto:mark "Appraise" DOWN
RIGHT*3
@cursorto:mark "Concentration" DOWN
RIGHT*3
ENTER y

a       # Personality archetype
@while "Learn which spell" a

ESC     # dismiss the arrival-room description; now in play
w       # wizard mode
y       # "Enter wizard mode?" -- yes
w       # [w] Wizard Mode Switches
DOWN DOWN
SPACE   # Free Advancement: NO -> YES
ESC

d                               # character sheet

# Four levels, one G at a time, each followed by the two menus a mage level
# can open. "Press G until the level shows" does not work: those menus cover
# the sheet, so the level never becomes visible, and 'g' is itself a menu
# letter, so the stray presses pick spells at random.
G
@while "Learn which spell" a
@while "Choose a bonus metamagic" a
G
@while "Learn which spell" a
@while "Choose a bonus metamagic" a
G
@while "Learn which spell" a
@while "Choose a bonus metamagic" a
G
@while "Learn which spell" a
@while "Choose a bonus metamagic" a
G
@while "Learn which spell" a
@while "Choose a bonus metamagic" a
G
@while "Learn which spell" a
@while "Choose a bonus metamagic" a
G
@while "Learn which spell" a
@while "Choose a bonus metamagic" a
G
@while "Learn which spell" a
@while "Choose a bonus metamagic" a
@expect "Mage 5"

# Four Knowledge skills to 10. ISkillLevel counts ranks, training and
# (attribute-11)/2, so four ranks apiece clears the bar with Intelligence 18.
S
@expect "Unspent Skill Ranks"
@cursorto:mark "Knowledge (Planes" DOWN
RIGHT*6
@cursorto:mark "Knowledge (Magic" UP
RIGHT*6
@cursorto:mark "Knowledge (Mytho" DOWN
RIGHT*6
@cursorto:mark "Knowledge (Nature" DOWN
RIGHT*6
ENTER y

# Ten levels of Divination: 3 + 3 + 2 + 2.
@until "HP:" ESC
w
@choose "Learn Any Spell"
"Clairvoyance" ENTER
w
@choose "Learn Any Spell"
"Magic Mapping" ENTER
w
@choose "Learn Any Spell"
"Detect Objects" ENTER
w
@choose "Learn Any Spell"
"Identify" ENTER

@until "Skill Ratings" d
P                               # [P]restige Classes
@expect "Choose a class:"
@choose "Loremaster"
@expect "Loremaster 0"          # the gate let him in

# Five levels. Each level-up opens "Which class do you wish to advance in?",
# and G is pressed until it does rather than once, because a stray message
# window -- "You feel luckier." -- can eat the first press.
# because the character has two classes, so the answer is given by name. The
# Loremaster also hands over a book at 2nd and 4th level; it lands in the
# In-the-Air slot and the game will not leave inventory mode while anything
# is there, so it has to be stowed before any other key is spent.
@until "class do you wish to advance" G
@choose "Loremaster"
@while "Learn which spell" a
@while "Choose a feat" a
ESC
@while "Air':?" s
@while "ESC:Done" ESC
@until "Skill Ratings" d
@until "class do you wish to advance" G
@choose "Loremaster"
@while "Learn which spell" a
@while "Choose a feat" a
ESC
@while "Air':?" s
@while "ESC:Done" ESC
@until "Skill Ratings" d
@until "class do you wish to advance" G
@choose "Loremaster"
@while "Learn which spell" a
@while "Choose a feat" a
ESC
@while "Air':?" s
@while "ESC:Done" ESC
@until "Skill Ratings" d
@until "class do you wish to advance" G
@choose "Loremaster"
@while "Learn which spell" a
@while "Choose a feat" a
ESC
@while "Air':?" s
@while "ESC:Done" ESC
@until "Skill Ratings" d
@until "class do you wish to advance" G
@choose "Loremaster"
@while "Learn which spell" a
@while "Choose a feat" a
ESC
@while "Air':?" s
@while "ESC:Done" ESC
@until "Skill Ratings" d
@expect "Loremaster 5"

# THE MEASUREMENT. Two Manuals of Gainful Exercise, acquired through wizard
# mode with the plus TYPED IN as 1 rather than rolled, so each one gives a
# fixed base of exactly 1 point. A reader without the ability therefore ends
# on +2 inherent Strength, and on nothing else. A Loremaster of 5th level or
# better ends on +2 plus two rolls of 1d2, so between +4 and +6. The two
# ranges do not touch.
#
# WHY THE PLUS IS 1 AND NOT MORE. Creature::GainInherentBonus caps the total
# at 5 + CA_INHERANT_POTENTIAL (src/Creature.cpp:1950), and a human carries
# +3 of that ability (lib/races.irh:205), so this character saturates at +8.
# Three tomes at plus 2 reach the cap with or without the fix and measure
# nothing. Two at plus 1 top out at +6, inside it.
#
# The tomes are taken one at a time rather than both at once, because the
# pack stacks them: two in hand are drawn "2 Manuals of Gainful Exercise",
# and @choose matches a name from its start. One at a time the name is always
# the same, and reading a tome destroys it (lib/m_items.irh:56) before the
# next one is acquired.
#
# The read command is lowercase 'r'. Uppercase would be wrong: the key tables
# store { KY_CMD_READ, 'R', 0 } with no modifier flag, and StandardKeySet
# matches toupper(ch) against the raw key and then compares the flags
# exactly, so shift+R matches nothing at all.
@until "HP:" ESC
w
@choose "Item Acquisition"
@until "]: Tomes" RIGHT
ENTER
"1" ENTER                       # the tome's plus, so the base gain is fixed
@while "Air':Manual" s          # stow it; the game will not leave inventory
@while "ESC:Done" ESC           #   mode while the In-the-Air slot is full
r
@choose "(in pack) Manual of Gainful Exercise"
@while "--More--" ENTER
w
@choose "Item Acquisition"
@until "]: Tomes" RIGHT
ENTER
"1" ENTER                       # the tome's plus, so the base gain is fixed
@while "Air':Manual" s          # stow it; the game will not leave inventory
@while "ESC:Done" ESC           #   mode while the In-the-Air slot is full
r
@choose "(in pack) Manual of Gainful Exercise"
@while "--More--" ENTER

@until "Skill Ratings" d
@dump:sheet
@until "HP:" ESC
@quit
